# Gate step 1077-vzwq — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# scripts/test-trace-coverage.sh was one of the orphan fixtures 1063-nraf
# measured: present, maintained, and invoked by nothing. Binding it IS its
# disposal.
#
# WHAT IT DOES AND DOES NOT COVER, because the last two things said about this
# file turned out to be wrong in the same direction:
#
#   IT DOES pin the validator's argument handling, its PASS/FAIL implication,
#   its failure path (exit code, the uncovered listing by NAME, the action
#   trailer), its default threshold, and that its denominator matches the number
#   of spec directories that actually exist.
#
#   IT DOES NOT guard the 1069-c9w6 SIGPIPE regression. Two of its arms appeared
#   to and did not: they were firing on grep's rc=2 error path, produced only
#   because the synthetic tree omitted three of the five roots the validator
#   greps. With the tree made faithful, reverting that fix leaves this fixture
#   green while the live tree reports 98% / 174-of-177. Nothing else catches it
#   either — filed as 1084-nzqc.
#
# It adds NO coverage floor. Exactly one arm touches the real checkout, at
# --coverage-threshold 0, which no coverage figure can fail; the earlier version
# of this file required the live tree to PASS at 80 and would have wired an
# undeclared floor into every host's gate. The project's one real live floor
# stays where it is, in scripts/local-ci.sh.
#
# On a host without jq three arms self-skip and the run is 9 of 12, printing
# `skip:test-trace-coverage:no-jq`. Nothing in --check counts that token yet.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose: a binding assembled from a
# variable is invisible to every name-based scan, including the
# bound-or-retired guard (1063-nraf). Keep it a plain string.
STEP_DESC="Checking the trace-coverage validator's thresholds, failure path and denominator (1077-vzwq)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-trace-coverage.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the trace-coverage validator mis-handles a threshold, mis-reports its failure path, or its denominator disagrees with the specs on disk (1077-vzwq) — see the verdict line above"
STEP_OK="Trace-coverage validator check passed"
